, and repeats. You wake up in the morning to a log of experiments and (hopefully) a better model. The training code here is a simplified single-GPU implementation of cite89†nanochat . The core idea is that you're not touching any of the Python files like you normally would as a researcher.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHY-WorldPlay/worldcompass/README.md at main · Tencent-Hunyuan/HY-WorldPlay · GitHub (https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/HY-WorldPlay/blob/main/worldcompass/README.md)\nciteturn32168view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn32167view0\",\"id\":102}); Total lines: 435\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2602.09022] WorldCompass: Reinforcement Learning for Long-Horizon World Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09022)\nciteturn32168view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn32167view0\",\"id\":103}); Total lines: 161\n"
